```java
// Serveur
try (ServerSocket serveur = new ServerSocket(5050)) {
    Socket client = serveur.accept();          // bloque jusqu'à une connexion
    BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(client.getInputStream()));
    PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(client.getOutputStream(), true);
    String reponse = in.readLine();
    out.println("Reçu : " + reponse);
}

// Client
try (Socket s = new Socket("192.168.1.20", 5050)) {
    PrintWriter out = new PrintWriter(s.getOutputStream(), true);
    BufferedReader in = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(s.getInputStream()));
    out.println("B");
    System.out.println(in.readLine());
}
```

- `accept()` **bloque** jusqu'à ce qu'un client arrive.
- Il faut un **protocole** : un format de messages convenu (ex. `REPONSE;3;B`).
